101
00:06:03,000 --> 00:06:04,704
So when it comes to trend trading,

102
00:06:04,704 --> 00:06:06,408
right, one of the most important things

103
00:06:06,408 --> 00:06:08,599
to remember is that the base is your friend.

104
00:06:09,000 --> 00:06:10,100
Everyone says, oh, the trend is your friend.

105
00:06:10,100 --> 00:06:11,500
Really, the base is your friend.

106
00:06:13,600 --> 00:06:18,700
The trend is more of your group of friends, but the base is your best friend.

107
00:06:19,700 --> 00:06:24,200
And the reason for this is the base represents the point at which buyers and sellers are most evenly matched.

108
00:06:24,900 --> 00:06:27,334
As the market starts to move in one direction or

109
00:06:27,334 --> 00:06:29,038
the other, there'll be more buyers than

110
00:06:29,038 --> 00:06:30,498
sellers or more sellers than buyers.

111
00:06:31,000 --> 00:06:32,800
But at the base, they are balanced.

112
00:06:34,300 --> 00:06:36,480
Remember, markets move from balance to imbalance,

113
00:06:36,480 --> 00:06:42,398
and it's when that move is happening, that imbalance area, that's when you can make a lot of money.

114
00:06:43,900 --> 00:06:48,600
If you can identify that, yeah, we're forming a base and now the market is moving to imbalance.

115
00:06:48,900 --> 00:06:55,900
So it's important to stay close to the base because that's where you're most likely to find support or resistance.

116
00:06:56,100 --> 00:06:58,722
So next time you are trend trading, you know, trying to look

117
00:06:58,722 --> 00:07:00,033
for trends, remember to keep your

118
00:07:00,033 --> 00:07:01,999
friends close by the base and trade around it.

119
00:07:02,500 --> 00:07:07,400
You want to be able to identify that base, you know, that we're coming down forming a base.

120
00:07:07,900 --> 00:07:09,900
The opposite would be true if we're coming into a swing high.

121
00:07:10,000 --> 00:07:12,600
Are we forming a base at a high?

122
00:07:13,500 --> 00:07:15,988
But anytime you have a sell-off, look for

123
00:07:15,988 --> 00:07:18,476
a base to start forming, just as anytime

124
00:07:18,476 --> 00:07:21,898
you have a rally, look for a base to start forming.

125
00:07:22,400 --> 00:07:26,200
So if you're trend trading, then the base is your friend.

126
00:07:26,900 --> 00:07:29,400
When prices are in a downtrend, the lows form the base.

127
00:07:29,400 --> 00:07:32,000
When prices are in an uptrend, the highs form the base.

128
00:07:32,600 --> 00:07:34,311
And I know that's probably not

129
00:07:34,311 --> 00:07:36,022
the proper terminology because you think

130
00:07:36,022 --> 00:07:37,733
